.TH "cbor::sequence_reader" 3 "Version 0.9.0" "mbedded-cbor" \" -*- nroff -*-
.ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
cbor::sequence_reader \- Reads a CBOR sequence (RFC 8742) whose bytes arrive in pieces, for example from a socket\&.  

.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.PP
\fR#include <cbor/sequence_reader\&.hpp>\fP
.SS "Public Member Functions"

.in +1c
.ti -1c
.RI "\fBsequence_reader\fP ()=default"
.br
.RI "Makes a reader that holds no byte\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "\fBsequence_reader\fP (sequence_reader const &)=delete"
.br
.ti -1c
.RI "\fBsequence_reader\fP & \fBoperator=\fP (\fBsequence_reader\fP const &)=delete"
.br
.ti -1c
.RI "\fBsequence_reader\fP (sequence_reader &&other)=default"
.br
.RI "Takes the bytes and the state of \fRother\fP\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "\fBsequence_reader\fP & \fBoperator=\fP (\fBsequence_reader\fP &&other)=default"
.br
.RI "Takes the bytes and the state of \fRother\fP\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "template<borrowed_range_of_chars Piece>"
.br
requires (!std::is_array_v<Piece>)
.br
void \fBfeed\fP (Piece const piece)
.br
.RI "Copies the bytes of a view to the end of the sequence\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "template<owning_range_of_chars Piece>"
.br
requires (!std::is_array_v<Piece>)
.br
void \fBfeed\fP (Piece const &piece)
.br
.RI "Copies the bytes of a container to the end of the sequence\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "template<owning_range_of_chars Piece> void \fBfeed\fP (Piece &&piece)"
.br
.RI "Takes a container by move and holds it as the next bytes of the sequence\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "template<owning_range_of_chars Piece> void \fBfeed\fP (std::shared_ptr< Piece const > piece)"
.br
.RI "Holds the bytes of \fRpiece\fP as the next bytes of the sequence, without a copy\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "bool \fBempty\fP () const"
.br
.RI "Tells if the reader holds no byte that no item took\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "std::expected< \fBlazy\fP, \fBerror\fP > \fBnext\fP ()"
.br
.RI "Gives the next item when all of its bytes are there\&. "
.in -1c
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP 
Reads a CBOR sequence (RFC 8742) whose bytes arrive in pieces, for example from a socket\&. 

\fR\fBfeed\fP\fP gives the reader the next piece\&. \fR\fBnext\fP\fP gives the next item as a \fBcbor::lazy\fP when all of its bytes are there, and \fRtoo_little_data\fP while it waits\&. \fR\fBempty\fP\fP is true when the reader holds no byte that no item took\&.

.PP
\fRfeed(std::move(s))\fP takes a \fRstd::string\fP by move\&. \fRfeed(shared_ptr)\fP holds the piece without a copy\&. \fRfeed(view)\fP and \fRfeed(s)\fP copy the bytes\&. An item that is whole in a piece that the reader holds is a view into that piece\&. The reader copies an item that the end of a piece cuts, and only the bytes of that item\&. Each item keeps its bytes alive after later feeds and after the reader is gone\&.

.PP
A char array, such as a literal, does not compile, because it holds a NUL after its last byte\&. A \fRstd::shared_ptr\fP to bytes that are not const does not compile\&. The reader cannot be copied\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
bytes: 82 01 02 03
call: cbor::sequence_reader r
result: sequence_reader that holds no unread byte
call: auto first = bytes\&.substr(0, 2)
result: 2 bytes: 82 01
call: r\&.feed(std::move(first))
result: void
call: r\&.empty()
result: false
call: auto second = bytes\&.substr(2)
result: 2 bytes: 02 03
call: r\&.feed(std::move(second))
result: void
call: r\&.next()\->size()
result: 2
call: r\&.next()\->get<std::int64_t>()
result: 3
call: r\&.empty()
result: true
.fi
.PP

.PP
\fBReturn values\fP
.RS 4
\fItoo_little_data\fP the item is not complete yet; feed more bytes 
.br
\fIsyntax_error\fP the bytes are not a well-formed item 
.br
\fIindefinite_length\fP a head uses indefinite length 
.RE
.PP
\fBExceptions\fP
.RS 4
\fIstd::logic_error\fP a null \fRstd::shared_ptr\fP, or a call on a reader that was moved from
.RE
.PP
After an error other than \fRtoo_little_data\fP, every call of \fR\fBnext\fP\fP gives that error, and \fR\fBfeed\fP\fP keeps no byte\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
    cbor::sequence_reader r;
    r\&.feed(std::move(first));       // 82 01: the start of [1, 2]
    auto const waiting = r\&.next();  // too_little_data
    r\&.feed(std::move(second));      // 02 03
    auto const pair = r\&.next();     // [1, 2]
    auto const three = r\&.next();    // 3
.fi
.PP
 
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBcbor::sequence\fP 

.PP
\fBcbor::lazy\fP 
.RE
.PP

